{
  "_about": "The attacks (grips, strikes, holds) a technique starts from: what they are called, who stands where, which hand takes what, and from which side. Read by src/posing/Attacks.gd, listed in docs/attacks.md. Positions are metres in Tori's frame: x is Tori's LEFT, y up, z forward (Tori faces +z). Hands are offsets from the character's own shoulder in its own frame. A grip's hand meets its target from the side the gripping forearm comes from (palm on the side of a wrist, thumb up), which Staging works out from Uke's shoulder; 'along' is where on the bone (0 its joint, 1 the next), 'curl' how far the fingers close. Names differ between schools and dojos; the ones marked 'check' are the compiler's best knowledge, not the instructor's — edit them here and the panel, the tool and the document follow. 'skews' lists the angles (degrees) the fingers may run across the bone at, tried in turn; square to it when absent.",
